To update the rendered template when the button is clicked, you can make an AJAX request to the backend view when the button is clicked, and then update the DOM with the response you receive.

Here's a step-by-step guide on how you can achieve this:

1. Create a button in your Django template that triggers the AJAX request. You can use a JavaScript function to make the AJAX request when the button is clicked. For example:
```html
button id="my-button"Click me!/button

script
