    const xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();
    xhr.open('GET', '/my-view/');
    xhr.onload = function () {
      if (xhr.status === 200) {
        const response = JSON.parse(xhr.responseText);
        // Update the DOM with the response data
        document.getElementById('result').innerHTML = response.html_template;
      } else {
        console.error('Request failed. Returned status of ' + xhr.status);
      }
    };
    xhr.send();
  }
/script
```
In this example, we're using an XMLHttpRequest object to make a GET request to the view at /my-view/ when the button is clicked. We're parsing the response text as JSON and using it to update the DOM element with id 'result'.

1. Modify your view to return the data in JSON format instead of rendering the template directly. For example:
